        <mxCell id="c148" value="&lt;i&gt;Report view, page Credits Cycle of Audit Monitoring (the text box with the written answer, below the table, is not drawn). The matrix gives, for each new test, the exceptions, the population and the rate per 1,000 by year and over the three years; the Total row&#x27;s population and rate are blank (outlined in coral) because the Population measure reads one process at a time. The cards count the register: 992 exceptions, of which 15 are reviewed, 841 mapped to a finding (outlined in teal, as in the table), 136 open, as before the four tests, and 2 findings open (in coral, with the status column that names the first step each has not met: no fix, retest or closure approval is recorded, and a target date reached would not close one). In amber, the date each finding covers through (12/31/2026) and its target date (12/31/2027): exceptions dated later, or not yet mapped, stay open for review.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="499" width="860" height="98" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
